CDX6020 hazard-vs-shape control, COMPILER-16.

Compile this chapter and read the WARNINGS, not the output. There is no
test mechanism for a warning in this tree -- codex/test/errors holds no
.expected files and nothing anywhere declares a warning -- which is why
this lives here rather than in codex/test, and why the behaviour below is
measured and NOT gated (L-NOGATE).

  before (shape detector, seed 42ACED00)
    CDX6020 on field 'a'
    CDX6020 on field 'b'

  after (hazard detector)
    CDX6020 on field 'a'

Field 'a' mutates c and field 'b' is evaluated AFTER and reads c, so 'a'
is the genuine hazard and must keep firing; in 'safe' the read precedes
the write, so it must not. A change that silences BOTH has made the check
vacuous, which is the failure this control exists to catch.

  partial traversal (seed 75B414046BEE5208)
    CDX6020 line 15 field 'a'

  complete traversal (COMPILER-71)
    CDX6020 line 15 field 'a'
    CDX6020 line 32 field 'a'

hazard-in-list is the arm that separates the two, and it was added because
the first two cannot: both reach the read of c through AFieldAccess, which
the partial traversal already handled, so both agree whichever traversal is
installed. Its read sits in a list literal, which was one of eleven AExpr
variants the partial search answered False for. Neither traversal fires on
'safe', so the widening did not cost the narrowing that took this check from
13 sites to 1.
